            "en": {
              "mode": "text",
              "body": "Lean builds proof irrelevance into definitional equality: any two proofs of the same proposition are treated as equal by the kernel. Other CIC-style systems may expose proof irrelevance differently or require an additional principle. In either case, proof irrelevance is not a consequence of impredicativity alone and should not be used to define impredicativity.",
